(3497101, 487617, 76198, '<td valign="top">I love these shots but I feel like the contrast is a little too high; you lose some of the sense of motion in the background and the clear delineation between the car and the background, they kind of blur together.</td>', 'I love these shots but I feel like the contrast is a little too high; you lose some of the sense of motion in the background and the clear delineation between the car and the background, they kind of blur together.', '2007-03-29 15:30:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497243, 486997, 61651, '<td valign="top">Wonderfully abstract.  Meets the challenge very well.</td>', 'Wonderfully abstract.  Meets the challenge very well.', '2007-03-29 16:23:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497244, 489491, 61651, '<td valign="top">Great pose and composition, great idea for meeting the challenge.  I really am impressed with how you captured the textures of the clothing - I guess this is down to the lighting?</td>', 'Great pose and composition, great idea for meeting the challenge.  I really am impressed with how you captured the textures of the clothing - I guess this is down to the lighting?', '2007-03-29 16:25:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497253, 489367, 61651, '<td valign="top">I like this - it''s just a simple, but unique composition.  Isolating the pinwheel in a studio shot is a good move, IMO - no distracting background, and the choice of colors are attractive</td>', 'I like this - it''s just a simple, but unique composition.  Isolating the pinwheel in a studio shot is a good move, IMO - no distracting background, and the choice of colors are attractive', '2007-03-29 16:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497264, 487852, 61651, '<td valign="top">Wow, what is that?  Very nice meet-the-challenge, and the wheel just pops out from the background.  I especially like that you can see the cityscape through the wheel, too.  It''s a shame the trees break up the full circle of the wheel, but I suppose that couldn''t be avoided.</td>', 'Wow, what is that?  Very nice meet-the-challenge, and the wheel just pops out from the background.  I especially like that you can see the cityscape through the wheel, too.  It''s a shame the trees break up the full circle of the wheel, but I suppose that couldn''t be avoided.', '2007-03-29 16:29:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497272, 488235, 61651, '<td valign="top">I like the view of the landscape through the turning propeller.  A clever take on the challenge.</td>', 'I like the view of the landscape through the turning propeller.  A clever take on the challenge.', '2007-03-29 16:31:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497280, 487849, 61651, '<td valign="top">I really like the pose and expression of the boy - it really expresses exhilaration well and meets the challenge.</td>', 'I really like the pose and expression of the boy - it really expresses exhilaration well and meets the challenge.', '2007-03-29 16:33:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497292, 487873, 60862, '<td valign="top">Heh.  I wondered whether anyone would try Spin the Bottle.  They''re Amazons compared to him!</td>', 'Heh.  I wondered whether anyone would try Spin the Bottle.  They''re Amazons compared to him!', '2007-03-29 16:36:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497322, 489185, 42013, '<td valign="top">I''m guessing it''s not Zoomdak, maybe a neighbor. A super idea for the challenge and one I am curious about. My only negative is the extreme amount of noise in the sky/ground. Unfortunately this will probably hurt your photo''s score. Still, a great idea and one that you could refine if you try it again. 7<br/> <br/>I''m guessing a flashlight tied to a rope and twirled while running away from the camera????</td>', 'I''m guessing it''s not Zoomdak, maybe a neighbor. A super idea for the challenge and one I am curious about. My only negative is the extreme amount of noise in the sky/ground. Unfortunately this will probably hurt your photo''s score. Still, a great idea and one that you could refine if you try it again. 7 I''m guessing a flashlight tied to a rope and twirled while running away from the camera????', '2007-03-29 16:40:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497373, 487987, 61651, '<td valign="top">This is a nice idea, especially with the capture of the reflection, but the composition might have been improved as a landscape orientation (to emphasize the  width of the carousel, and framing it so the carousel''s reflection wasn''t cut off on the end.  A good capture of the spinning lights.</td>', 'This is a nice idea, especially with the capture of the reflection, but the composition might have been improved as a landscape orientation (to emphasize the  width of the carousel, and framing it so the carousel''s reflection wasn''t cut off on the end.  A good capture of the spinning lights.', '2007-03-29 16:49:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497718, 489134, 67237, '<td valign="top">Very clever and perfectly executed idea. This should ribbon.<br/>I wish most of viewers (or should I say enough voting viewers to get the score this shot deserves) take their time to realize how this shot shows the spinning motion of the planet. Good luck on that!.I will take away 1 point because there is a bit too much softenning filter for my taste..(9)<br/>One more thing..it would be great to know: a) the coordinates of the place you took the shot from; b) where is the centre of the lense aiming to, north or south pole?</td>', 'Very clever and perfectly executed idea. This should ribbon.I wish most of viewers (or should I say enough voting viewers to get the score this shot deserves) take their time to realize how this shot shows the spinning motion of the planet. Good luck on that!.I will take away 1 point because there is a bit too much softenning filter for my taste..(9)One more thing..it would be great to know: a) the coordinates of the place you took the shot from; b) where is the centre of the lense aiming to, north or south pole?', '2007-03-29 18:20:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497720, 488416, 67237, '<td valign="top">great capture</td>', 'great capture', '2007-03-29 18:20:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497727, 489246, 67237, '<td valign="top">it would have been great to be able to see the actual spinning of those prop''s</td>', 'it would have been great to be able to see the actual spinning of those prop''s', '2007-03-29 18:23:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497731, 489500, 65964, '<td valign="top">hehe! Yes!! i love it !Love this idea, well framed and no doubt spinning.</td>', 'hehe! Yes!! i love it !Love this idea, well framed and no doubt spinning.', '2007-03-29 18:26:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497816, 489386, 60698, '<td valign="top">This looks like a winner! :)</td>', 'This looks like a winner! :)', '2007-03-29 19:09:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497868, 489525, 66515, '<td valign="top">Great colors and use of contre-jour. I''d like to see the top part of the sky lightened a bit so we see more detail in the upper part of the windmill. <br/> <br/>Perhaps converting the whole image to purple would be effective as well. (I''d like to see a sample later). <br/> <br/>Nice use of a longer exposure to show motion. <br/> <br/> <br/>Composition: It could be better but I can also see you were trying to line up the sun with the center of the windmill so your options were fairly limited. Nevertheless, the oblque lines created by the fin do create some nice drama in the shot. <br/> <br/>The challenge: This definitely fits the challenge. Furthermore it does so in an interesting way.</td>', 'Great colors and use of contre-jour. I''d like to see the top part of the sky lightened a bit so we see more detail in the upper part of the windmill.  Perhaps converting the whole image to purple would be effective as well. (I''d like to see a sample later).  Nice use of a longer exposure to show motion.   Composition: It could be better but I can also see you were trying to line up the sun with the center of the windmill so your options were fairly limited. Nevertheless, the oblque lines created by the fin do create some nice drama in the shot.  The challenge: This definitely fits the challenge. Furthermore it does so in an interesting way.', '2007-03-29 19:34:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497886, 488243, 66515, '<td valign="top">Interesting colors in this shot. I''d like to see a bit more saturation in the vegetation and especially the sky but as it is its alright. <br/> <br/>The motion of the subject is well portrayed and captured. The positioning of her arms and legs create a feeling of implied movement, while the flowing scarves and hair give us a more obvious sign of motion.<br/> <br/>Composition: The placing of the main subject is perfect. While perhaps not composed using the rule of thirds, her motion does seem to make it appear that way.  The leading lines of the stalks takes you into the frame and creates depth nicely. <br/> <br/>The challenge:<br/>Creative approach to the challenge and one that is quite unique. The setup and locale also aid in giving this a lot of originality.</td>', 'Interesting colors in this shot. I''d like to see a bit more saturation in the vegetation and especially the sky but as it is its alright.  The motion of the subject is well portrayed and captured. The positioning of her arms and legs create a feeling of implied movement, while the flowing scarves and hair give us a more obvious sign of motion. Composition: The placing of the main subject is perfect. While perhaps not composed using the rule of thirds, her motion does seem to make it appear that way.  The leading lines of the stalks takes you into the frame and creates depth nicely.  The challenge:Creative approach to the challenge and one that is quite unique. The setup and locale also aid in giving this a lot of originality.', '2007-03-29 19:39:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497892, 488858, 66515, '<td valign="top">Creative approach however this does appear to be lacking some focus. I can''t really see what the camera autofocused on if anything to be honest. <br/> <br/>There is a lot of noise that does distract from this image as well. <br/> <br/>The colors are nice and well saturated. The shape of the bamboo does create visual interest. <br/> <br/>The challenge: Certainly a unique take on this challenge. While there is isn''t actually motion in this capture, the shape of the bamboo creates a sort of visual movement throughout the frame thus meeting the challenge nicely.</td>', 'Creative approach however this does appear to be lacking some focus. I can''t really see what the camera autofocused on if anything to be honest.  There is a lot of noise that does distract from this image as well.  The colors are nice and well saturated. The shape of the bamboo does create visual interest.  The challenge: Certainly a unique take on this challenge. While there is isn''t actually motion in this capture, the shape of the bamboo creates a sort of visual movement throughout the frame thus meeting the challenge nicely.', '2007-03-29 19:42:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497902, 488323, 66515, '<td valign="top">lol...its been a while since I''ve seen this. (My shot of this got corrupted and I only ended up with half of the wheel). <br/> <br/>Nice colors and use a long exposure to create motion. There are a lot of distracting elements in the background however. <br/> <br/>The composition Positioning yourself closer and looking up might create more visual appeal. It would also get rid of a lot of the busy background.  Putting the center of the wheel in the middle of the frame is somewhat boring. An off center position would create visual drama.<br/> <br/>The challenge: Right on. You can''t say this DNMC at all. I don''t suspect there will be a lot of Toys R'' Us Times Square pictures entered either so this is quite unique. <br/> <br/>As an aside this is far better than the picture I took.</td>', 'lol...its been a while since I''ve seen this. (My shot of this got corrupted and I only ended up with half of the wheel).  Nice colors and use a long exposure to create motion. There are a lot of distracting elements in the background however.  The composition Positioning yourself closer and looking up might create more visual appeal. It would also get rid of a lot of the busy background.  Putting the center of the wheel in the middle of the frame is somewhat boring. An off center position would create visual drama. The challenge: Right on. You can''t say this DNMC at all. I don''t suspect there will be a lot of Toys R'' Us Times Square pictures entered either so this is quite unique.  As an aside this is far better than the picture I took.', '2007-03-29 19:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3497903, 489475, 45475, '<td valign="top">Fantastic. Love the rich browns and red tones. Excellent composition and point of view.</td>', 'Fantastic. Love the rich browns and red tones. Excellent composition and point of view.', '2007-03-29 19:47:16.000000', NULL, 1),
