(3518390, 489068, 42013, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by splidge:</b></div><hr/><i> Very nice shot, congratulations on the ribbon!<br/> <br/>I''m with you on the f/32 vs. dust thing.  Maybe get an ND filter?  I had a similar problem with my entry (although mine was at f/20 where the dust isn''t quite so bad). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I definitely could have used a ND! I already had a gradND but the white blades of the windmills against the dark sky were tough to hold. I still blew out the stationary ones.</td>', 'Originally posted by splidge: Very nice shot, congratulations on the ribbon! I''m with you on the f/32 vs. dust thing.  Maybe get an ND filter?  I had a similar problem with my entry (although mine was at f/20 where the dust isn''t quite so bad).   I definitely could have used a ND! I already had a gradND but the white blades of the windmills against the dark sky were tough to hold. I still blew out the stationary ones.', '2007-04-04 11:25:30.000000', NULL, 0),
