(3518852, 489475, 50695, '<td valign="top">I''m impressed. For someone who claims to not understand art, you seem able to cretae it. And judging from your description, it was deliberate. You picked the right picture and you made the right processing decisions.</td>', 'I''m impressed. For someone who claims to not understand art, you seem able to cretae it. And judging from your description, it was deliberate. You picked the right picture and you made the right processing decisions.', '2007-04-04 13:39:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3518910, 489475, 30982, '<td valign="top">Really, really nice work Jeff!  Looks like something I''d be proud to have taken, and better processed, too.</td>', 'Really, really nice work Jeff!  Looks like something I''d be proud to have taken, and better processed, too.', '2007-04-04 14:03:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3518936, 489475, 5792, '<td valign="top">Positives:<br/>Nicely captures the idea of spinning and childhood fun. The blur very nicely shows circular rotation and is its greatest strength.<br/> <br/>Technicals:<br/>The background hurts this image. You said, "would''ve brightened up the background, which I wanted to avoid, so I skipped it". Understood that you wanted the spinning child to stand out. Ironically, though, this may have helped reduced the score more than helped it because the BG is dark and has no interesting detail whatsoever to interest viewers. The BG is more distracting from your subject than supportive.<br/> <br/>Overall the image seems dark and oversaturated into the reds and browns. There is a distracting blue speck lower left of your subject. Might be slightly oversharpened.<br/> <br/>In motion blur images you want the still detail to be sharp and interesting for the viewer to look at and to provide a solid visual base for them WITHIN the image.<br/> <br/>The Challenge:<br/>No question. Meets the challenge very well. Overall technical quality affected your score more than challenge topic.<br/> <br/>Suggestions:<br/>The concept is great and you captured spinning very, very well. You just need to work on the technical quality of the image and add more supportive interest for viewers.<br/> <br/>Perhaps you could put a blanket or solid colored tarp of some kind on the ground under your subject and add a toy to improve viewer background interest. A complementary color like yellow might work well.<br/> <br/>Perhaps you did try and reject this, but a slightly longer shutter speed than 1/20th, maybe 1/10th or more, would work to. Back off on sharpening a bit and perhaps employ noise reduction to make the motion a little smoother. That can be tricky without making the rest of the image look ''plastic''.</td>', 'Positives:Nicely captures the idea of spinning and childhood fun. The blur very nicely shows circular rotation and is its greatest strength. Technicals:The background hurts this image. You said, "would''ve brightened up the background, which I wanted to avoid, so I skipped it". Understood that you wanted the spinning child to stand out. Ironically, though, this may have helped reduced the score more than helped it because the BG is dark and has no interesting detail whatsoever to interest viewers. The BG is more distracting from your subject than supportive. Overall the image seems dark and oversaturated into the reds and browns. There is a distracting blue speck lower left of your subject. Might be slightly oversharpened. In motion blur images you want the still detail to be sharp and interesting for the viewer to look at and to provide a solid visual base for them WITHIN the image. The Challenge:No question. Meets the challenge very well. Overall technical quality affected your score more than challenge topic. Suggestions:The concept is great and you captured spinning very, very well. You just need to work on the technical quality of the image and add more supportive interest for viewers. Perhaps you could put a blanket or solid colored tarp of some kind on the ground under your subject and add a toy to improve viewer background interest. A complementary color like yellow might work well. Perhaps you did try and reject this, but a slightly longer shutter speed than 1/20th, maybe 1/10th or more, would work to. Back off on sharpening a bit and perhaps employ noise reduction to make the motion a little smoother. That can be tricky without making the rest of the image look ''plastic''.', '2007-04-04 14:10:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3518950, 489306, 52352, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by noisemaker:</b></div><hr/><i> this reminds me of <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=68346" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">dainmcgowan</a> shot<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=482153" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/646/thumb/482153.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/646/thumb/482153.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/646/thumb/482153.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Woaaa I''m confused that looks like the same exact shot</td>', 'Originally posted by noisemaker: this reminds me of  dainmcgowan shot    Woaaa I''m confused that looks like the same exact shot', '2007-04-04 14:12:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519000, 489185, 9462, '<td valign="top">I like the grain, adds to the surreal feeling of being in a wormhole.</td>', 'I like the grain, adds to the surreal feeling of being in a wormhole.', '2007-04-04 14:25:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519050, 487413, 24454, '<td valign="top">That is such a cool title for this photo.  I love that song alot.  I love Neil Young''s version -- and my son is a total Phish Phreak!!!  I was afraid at one point he was going to drop out of college and follow them around the country like the Dead Heads used to do :)<br/> <br/>Anyway, that is exactly the mood this photo conveys.   I love it -- ALOT!!!!</td>', 'That is such a cool title for this photo.  I love that song alot.  I love Neil Young''s version -- and my son is a total Phish Phreak!!!  I was afraid at one point he was going to drop out of college and follow them around the country like the Dead Heads used to do :) Anyway, that is exactly the mood this photo conveys.   I love it -- ALOT!!!!', '2007-04-04 14:37:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519112, 488072, 24454, '<td valign="top">What a cool technique!  Man.  With the shutter only open .6 of a second, you must have been spinning that succer at break-neck speed.  I''m impressed, and think this turned out very well!<br/> <br/></td>', 'What a cool technique!  Man.  With the shutter only open .6 of a second, you must have been spinning that succer at break-neck speed.  I''m impressed, and think this turned out very well! ', '2007-04-04 14:51:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519124, 488081, 24454, '<td valign="top">Oh, I think this is very cool!   It reminds me of one of those digital art, abstract photos that I am growing more and more drawn to! <br/> <br/>Kudos!  And booo to the dumb voters who only gave this a 4.9!</td>', 'Oh, I think this is very cool!   It reminds me of one of those digital art, abstract photos that I am growing more and more drawn to!  Kudos!  And booo to the dumb voters who only gave this a 4.9!', '2007-04-04 14:56:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519159, 489497, 24454, '<td valign="top">Ohmy. . what a fun photo!  She looks like she is having such a delightful time.  I LOVE photos like this.   They stay in your heart long after a dumb challenge is long forgotten!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Ohmy. . what a fun photo!  She looks like she is having such a delightful time.  I LOVE photos like this.   They stay in your heart long after a dumb challenge is long forgotten! ', '2007-04-04 15:04:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519169, 488873, 5792, '<td valign="top">Positives:<br/>Wonderful perspective and the sharpness of your model looking into the dryer is good. It is the central subject of the composition. It is a nice touch and makes this image interesting. Curious expression and placement of the eye is perfect. Distribution of the laundry is good.<br/> <br/>Technicals:<br/>Overall technicals OK. Sharpness is fine, there are no digital artifacts which are normally the biggest defects in DPC images. There are some overexposed highlights your model''s head and arm and an object on the far left side that is distracting because it is unidentifiable.<br/> <br/>The Challenge:<br/>Ironically, though you had many concerns about meeting the challenge you were probably still nixed for it. That is because there was no ''actual'' motion and it is obvious in the composition.<br/> <br/>Perhaps the fact that the model and not spinning is the central subject hurt it in voting as well.<br/> <br/>Here is a funny... I tried to be metaphorical in my spinning image and got trashed for it. LOL!!! You are ALWAYS better to take as literal an interpretation of a challenge topic as you can. Yours, and mine, were NOT literal enough.<br/> <br/>Suggestions:<br/>The overexposed areas are a problem. For a basic chalenge the only way that can be corrected would to somehow add additional light inside the dryer to balance lighting and decrease exposure.<br/> <br/>As done this image would never get a thumbs up from the dnmc crowd. The only way to do that is to capture actual rotation of the dryer drum.</td>', 'Positives:Wonderful perspective and the sharpness of your model looking into the dryer is good. It is the central subject of the composition. It is a nice touch and makes this image interesting. Curious expression and placement of the eye is perfect. Distribution of the laundry is good. Technicals:Overall technicals OK. Sharpness is fine, there are no digital artifacts which are normally the biggest defects in DPC images. There are some overexposed highlights your model''s head and arm and an object on the far left side that is distracting because it is unidentifiable. The Challenge:Ironically, though you had many concerns about meeting the challenge you were probably still nixed for it. That is because there was no ''actual'' motion and it is obvious in the composition. Perhaps the fact that the model and not spinning is the central subject hurt it in voting as well. Here is a funny... I tried to be metaphorical in my spinning image and got trashed for it. LOL!!! You are ALWAYS better to take as literal an interpretation of a challenge topic as you can. Yours, and mine, were NOT literal enough. Suggestions:The overexposed areas are a problem. For a basic chalenge the only way that can be corrected would to somehow add additional light inside the dryer to balance lighting and decrease exposure. As done this image would never get a thumbs up from the dnmc crowd. The only way to do that is to capture actual rotation of the dryer drum.', '2007-04-04 15:06:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519283, 487849, 5112, '<td valign="top">Many congratulations, Jason!  I like it very much how he looks so happy spinning like that, it''s good that way.<br/>My question though:  How in the world does he manage to keep his runners so sparkly clean?  My kid''s shoes were always messed up and dirty.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-04-04 14:41:13.</i></td>', 'Many congratulations, Jason!  I like it very much how he looks so happy spinning like that, it''s good that way.My question though:  How in the world does he manage to keep his runners so sparkly clean?  My kid''s shoes were always messed up and dirty.', '2007-04-04 15:39:46.000000', '2007-04-04 15:41:13.000000', 0),
(3519313, 488873, 60862, '<td valign="top">Ha!  Made me laugh. :)</td>', 'Ha!  Made me laugh. :)', '2007-04-04 15:47:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519368, 487849, 60195, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the Red, Doc! Fantastic image. With your short "ribbon-hiatus"... I was beginning to wonder if the 5D was such a good idea after-all  ;o)</td>', 'Congrats on the Red, Doc! Fantastic image. With your short "ribbon-hiatus"... I was beginning to wonder if the 5D was such a good idea after-all  ;o)', '2007-04-04 16:02:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519418, 488072, 40683, '<td valign="top">Ah, mall madness, captured...Love it!</td>', 'Ah, mall madness, captured...Love it!', '2007-04-04 16:13:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519464, 488052, 68514, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Spizzer:</b></div><hr/><i> I wonder how many will see this as a fishing spinner? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes...that''s the question about this shot :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Spizzer: I wonder how many will see this as a fishing spinner?  Yes...that''s the question about this shot :)', '2007-04-04 16:25:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519501, 488204, 5792, '<td valign="top">Positives:<br/>Simplicity, color and tones are the strengths of this image. Technically done very well. Off-centered composition adds viewer interest to the composition.<br/> <br/>Technicals:<br/>Technically quite good, especially the streaks that convey the sense of spinning that any viewer can easily see. Though the nature of this image does not have a lot of tonality, what it does have is very nice. Light and exposure is well balanced across the frame.<br/> <br/>The Challenge:<br/>No doubt, meets the challenge. <br/> <br/>Something unique among motion blur images is that the highest scoring ones usually have something in the frame that is sharply focused. The highest scoring images have sharp areas in the actually moving object. Yours has none of that.<br/> <br/>The image has a surrealistic, impressionistic feel but those type images typically do not fair well at DPC. That is to bad.<br/> <br/>This is a well conceived and executed image both photographically and technically but scored like its little more than garbage. That is not very satisfying when you put a lot of work into it. Don''t despair, you won''t hit a home run on every image.<br/> <br/>Suggestions:<br/>None. Perhaps the problem with this image is that voters thought it dull and uninteresting. Perhaps you, me and your mom are the only people that like it. ;)</td>', 'Positives:Simplicity, color and tones are the strengths of this image. Technically done very well. Off-centered composition adds viewer interest to the composition. Technicals:Technically quite good, especially the streaks that convey the sense of spinning that any viewer can easily see. Though the nature of this image does not have a lot of tonality, what it does have is very nice. Light and exposure is well balanced across the frame. The Challenge:No doubt, meets the challenge.  Something unique among motion blur images is that the highest scoring ones usually have something in the frame that is sharply focused. The highest scoring images have sharp areas in the actually moving object. Yours has none of that. The image has a surrealistic, impressionistic feel but those type images typically do not fair well at DPC. That is to bad. This is a well conceived and executed image both photographically and technically but scored like its little more than garbage. That is not very satisfying when you put a lot of work into it. Don''t despair, you won''t hit a home run on every image. Suggestions:None. Perhaps the problem with this image is that voters thought it dull and uninteresting. Perhaps you, me and your mom are the only people that like it. ;)', '2007-04-04 16:38:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519519, 489068, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by inshaala:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice shot and the rainbow tops it off (i sympathise with you about the dust - i think mine is probably the same) - although i wouldnt recommend a polarising filter for use with a rainbow, arent rainbows by essence polarised light? ND is the way to go :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not a problem, you can rotate the polarizer so it is NOT polarizing the rainbow and then it''s just a ND filter in effect.<br/> <br/>Great shot. Peters :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by inshaala: Nice shot and the rainbow tops it off (i sympathise with you about the dust - i think mine is probably the same) - although i wouldnt recommend a polarising filter for use with a rainbow, arent rainbows by essence polarised light? ND is the way to go :)   Not a problem, you can rotate the polarizer so it is NOT polarizing the rainbow and then it''s just a ND filter in effect. Great shot. Peters :-)', '2007-04-04 16:44:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519639, 489391, 30982, '<td valign="top">You look like you''re about 12 or 13 years old in this shot.  OK, <i>maybe</i> 16.  Quite like it.</td>', 'You look like you''re about 12 or 13 years old in this shot.  OK, maybe 16.  Quite like it.', '2007-04-04 17:18:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3519646, 488179, 30982, '<td valign="top">Title made the shot.  Wondering how many just didn''t get the connection?</td>', 'Title made the shot.  Wondering how many just didn''t get the connection?', '2007-04-04 17:19:35.000000', NULL, 0),
